    description: "WI-zizuf revealed that Gradle/Maven projects have near-zero external_dep nodes because external dependencies (Jackson, Netty, RocksDB, etc.) are declared in build.gradle/pom.xml but not physically present on disk. The file-path-based classifier can never classify them. Fix: extend DependencyManifest (currently Go-only via go.mod) to parse Gradle dependency declarations (implementation/api/compileOnly from build.gradle, libs.versions.toml) and Maven dependency declarations (pom.xml <dependencies>) so that classify_import() can classify unresolved Java/Kotlin imports as external_dep. This is a follow-up to the workspace detection fix in WI-zizuf — that fix improves first_party/internal_dep distinction within the project, but external deps remain invisible without manifest parsing."  # 5122
    fields: {}  # 5122
